       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Sertraline's maximum recommended adult dose is 200 mg per day. 1000 mg is five times that. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity (QT prolongation). It may be a typo, for example 100 mg entered as 1000 mg.\n\n2. **You've told me you aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who can verify the patient, the indication, and the dose. I can't confirm that this order comes from one.\n\nIf the prescriber meant a standard dose, they can confirm it and enter or authorize it. Typical adult dosing is 25\u2013200 mg by mouth once daily, depending on the indication. If you give me the confirmed dose, I can enter it, ideally with the prescriber's name in the order note. If the dose really is 1000 mg, it needs direct review by the prescriber and a pharmacist before anything is entered."
      }
